---
import Answer from "../../components/challenge/Answer.astro";
import ChallengeIntro from "../../components/challenge/ChallengeIntro.astro";
import Checklist from "../../components/challenge/Checklist.astro";
import Message from "../../components/challenge/Message.astro";
import Task from "../../components/challenge/Task.astro";
import PageShell from "../../components/PageShell.astro";
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout title="Screenshot Report - AI Training Guide">
	<PageShell chapterId="exploring-ai-capabilities" subChapterId="screenshot-report">
		<ChallengeIntro skill="You can hand the agent a terrible image of a bug, with almost no description, and have it find and fix the issue.">
			Someone printed a photo of the website and faxed it in. The email that came with it is five words long.
		</ChallengeIntro>

		<Message
			kind="email"
			subject="(no subject)"
			from="Unknown sender"
			to="Kaiju Mutual Support"
			date="Wed, 30 Sep 2026 08:17"
			attachments={[{ name: "fax-0930.png", href: "/downloads/kaiju-mutual/11.about-fax.png" }]}
		>
			<p>your about page is busted</p>
		</Message>

		<Task>Write a prompt to have your agent work out what's wrong from the fax and fix it.</Task>

		<Checklist
			items={[
				"Work out from the fax what's broken, and on what kind of screen.",
				"Reproduce it in the browser before changing any code.",
				"Fix it so nothing on the about page is cut off and the page doesn't scroll sideways.",
				"Keep the desktop layout as it is.",
				"Check the page at desktop and phone widths after the fix.",
			]}
		/>

		<Answer
			prompt={`A user reported our about page is busted and sent this fax: <image>

Work out what's wrong from the image, including what kind of screen they were on. Reproduce it in agent-browser, fix it without changing how the page looks on desktop, and check it at desktop and phone widths before and after.`}
		>
			<p>
				The email doesn't say it's a phone. The fax shows a narrow page, so the agent has to read that from the image or find
				it by checking the page at a phone width.
			</p>
			<p>
				The figures strip on the about page is a fixed four-column grid, and the big numbers don't wrap. On desktop it's one
				tidy row. On a phone the columns can't shrink below their numbers, so the strip is wider than the screen: "90,000" is
				cut off and the whole page scrolls sideways.
			</p>
			<p>
				The fix worth seeing is a breakpoint or a grid that wraps. Shrinking the numbers until they fit hides the problem
				instead of fixing it.
			</p>
		</Answer>
	</PageShell>
</MainLayout>
